hadiths[33]{hadithnumber,text}:
"923","to visit him when he is ill, to be with him when he dies, to accept when\nhe invites him, and to ask for mercy on him when he sneezes.\""924"""
"924","Muhammad ibn Salam narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Ahwas informed us, from Ash'ath, from Mu'awiyah ibn Suwayd, from Al-Bara' ibn Azib, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us with seven things and forbade us from seven. He commanded us: to visit the sick, to follow funerals, to say ""Yarhamuk Allah"" to one who sneezes, to fulfill oaths, to help the oppressed, to spread the greeting of peace, and to accept invitations. And he forbade us from: gold rings, silver vessels, mayathir (silk cushions), qasiyyah (a type of silk), istabraq (thick silk), dibaj (brocade), and silk."
"925","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \A Muslim owes another Muslim six duties.\""\nHe was asked"
"926","'Ali said, \When someone hears a sneeze and says"
"927","Abu Salih reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, said, \When one of you sneezes"
"928","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, said, \Allah loves the sneeze and dislikes yawning. When\none you sneezes and praises Allah"
"929","Ibn 'Abbas said, \When someone is wished mercy"
"930","Abu Hurayra said, \We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah"
"931","Adam narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Sulayman Al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas say: Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. He said \Yarhamuk Allah\"" (May Allah have mercy on you) to one of them"
"932","Abu Hurayra said, \Two men sat in the presence of the Prophet may\nAllah bless him and grant him peace"
"933","Nafi' said that when 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar sneezed, they said\nto him, \May Allah have mercy on you"
"934","'Abdullah said, \When one of you sneezes"
"935","Iyas ibn Salama related that his father said, \A man sneezed in\nthe presence of the Prophet"
"936","Makhul al-Azdi said, \I was beside Ibn 'Umar when a man sneezed\non one side of the mosque. Ibn 'Umar said"
"937","Mujahid said, \When a son of 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar"
"938","Abu al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, saying: Iyas ibn Salamah narrated to me, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a man sneezed. He said: ""May Allah have mercy on you."" Then he sneezed again. The Prophet ﷺ said: ""This man has a cold."""
"939","Abu Hurayra said, \Wish mercy on a person once"
"940","Abu Musa said, \The Jews used to sneeze in the presence of the\nProphet"
"941","Abu Burda said, \I came to Abu Musa while he was in the house of\nUmm al-Fadl ibn al-'Abbas and I sneezed and Abu Musa did not wish mercy\non me. Umm al-Fadl sneezed and he wished mercy on her. I told my mother"
"942","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, said, \When one of you yawns"
"943","Here is the translated text in English:Musa bin Isma'il narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from Mu'adh, who said: I was the companion of the Prophet, peace be upon him. He said: O Mu'adh, I said: I am at your service and ready to obey. Then he said the same thing three times: Do you know what is due to Allah upon His creation? I said: No, he said: That they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. Then he walked for a while and said: O Mu'adh, I said: I am at your service and ready to obey. He said: Do you know what is due to the creation upon Allah, the Exalted, the Glorious, if they do that? That He will not punish them."
"944","When Allah accepted my repentance \nand the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) announced at the time of the fajr prayers that Allah had accepted my repentance, people met me in large number and congratulated me on the acceptance of my repentance. They said, \Congratulations to you. Allah has approved your repentance.\"" And I entered the Masjid Nabawi. People were sitting around him. Talhah bin Ubayd Allah \nran towards me after standing up and shook hands with me and congratulated me. By Allah"
"945","Abu Sa’eed al-Khudri (ra) said that some people (the Jews of Banu Quraysh) came down at the command of Sa’d bin Mu’az . He was called and he came riding a donkey. When he approached the mosque, the Prophet (ﷺ) said, \Rise up for one better than you\"""
"946","Anas said, \There is no one that people loved to see more than\nthe Prophet"
"947","'A'isha, the Umm al-Mu'minin, said, \I have not seen anyone who\nmore resembled the Prophet"
"948","He narrated to us 'Abdullah bin Salah, who said: Al-Layth narrated to me, who said: Abu Zubair narrated to me from Jabir, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) fell ill, so we prayed behind him while he was sitting, and Abu Bakr was teaching the people to say ""Takbir"" (Allahu Akbar). He turned towards us and saw us standing, so he pointed to us and we sat down. We prayed with him in his sitting position, and when he finished, he said: ""If you were to do what the Persians and Romans do, they would rise against their kings while they are sitting, so do not do that. Be content with your imams, for if the imam is standing, stand with him, and if he is sitting, sit with him."""
"949","Abu Sa'id reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, said, \When one of you yawns"
"950","Ibn Abbas said, \When someone yawns"
"951","Musaddad narrated to us, saying: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, saying: Suhayl narrated to us, saying: I heard a son of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrating to his father, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""When one of you yawns, let him hold his mouth shut, for the devil enters it."" Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, saying: Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Suhayl narrated to me, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me, from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""When one of you yawns, let him hold his mouth with his hand, for the devil enters it."""
"952","He narrated to us 'Abdullah bin Yusuf, who said: Malik informed us, from Ishaq bin Abi Talhah, that he heard Anas bin Malik say: The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to enter upon Umm Haram, the daughter of Milhan, and she would feed him. She used to be at 'Ubada bin As-Samit's, and she would feed him and make his head wet, and then he would fall asleep, then wake up and laugh."
"953","Here is the translated text in English:

Ali bin Abdullah narrated to us, saying: Al-Mughirah bin Salamah, Abu Hisham al-Makhzumi, was a trustworthy narrator. He said: Al-Sa'iq bin Hazn narrated to us, saying: Al-Qasim bin Mutayyib narrated to us from Al-Hasan al-Basri, from Qays bin Asim al-Sa'di. He said: I visited the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and he said: This is the leader of the inhabitants of the desert. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the wealth that is not mine, and there is no one who is seeking it, nor is it from a guest? He said: The best wealth is 480, and most of it is 600. Woe to the companions of the meadows, except for those who have been given the most beautiful of the beautiful, and those who have been given the most abundant of the abundant, and those who have been given the most abundant of the abundant. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the most generous of these relationships? He said: How do you intend to give in charity? I said: I will give to the young, and I will give to the old. He said: How do you intend to give in charity in the time of drought? I said: I will give to the one who is in need. He said: How do you intend to give in charity in the time of abundance? He said: I will give to the one who is in need. He said: How do you intend to give in charity in the time of war? He said: The people will be destroyed by their own greed, and no one will be given a share of the spoils of war, and they will not be given a share of the spoils of war. He said: What is your wealth, is it dearer to you or is it dearer to your companions? I said: My wealth. He said: Then you have what you have eaten and what you have given, and the rest is for your companions. I said: I will not leave. If I return, I will make my companions rich. When death approached, he gathered his sons and said: O my sons, take from me. You will not take from anyone else, for you are more merciful to me than I am to you. Do not mourn for me, for the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) did not mourn for me. I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) forbidding mourning. You should bury me in my clothes, and you should mourn for your children. If you mourn for your children, it will be a burden on your parents. If you mourn for your children, it will be a burden on your parents."
"954","'Abdullah ibn as-Samit said, \I questioned my close friend Abu\nDharr who said"
"955","'Ali reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace, knocked at the door of 'Ali and Fatima, the daughter\nof the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and said, \Don't\nyou pray?\"" 'Ali said"
